\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every Noetherian regular local domain A with fraction field F, is the canonical map $K_{3}(A)\to K_{3}(F)$ injective on integral algebraic K-theory, including ramified mixed characteristic?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every Noetherian regular local domain A with fraction field F, is the canonical map $K_{3}(A)\to K_{3}(F)$ injective on integral algebraic K-theory, including ramified mixed characteristic?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-Integral-Degree-Three-Gersten-Counterexample-September-26-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

